4 | struct MyError;
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = note: implement `WebResponseError<St, St::Error>` for `MyError`, where `St` is the application state; the default `error_response()` returns 500
  = note: or wrap the error with a helper such as `web::error::ErrorBadRequest(err)`
  = help: the following other types implement trait `WebResponseError<St, Err>`:
            `!` implements `WebResponseError<St, Err>`
            `ClientPayloadError` implements `WebResponseError<St, DefaultError>`
            `ContentTypeError` implements `WebResponseError<St, DefaultError>`
            `DefaultError` implements `WebResponseError<St, DefaultError>`
            `HandshakeError` implements `WebResponseError<St, DefaultError>`
            `HttpError` implements `WebResponseError<St, DefaultError>`
            `InternalError<T>` implements `WebResponseError<St, Err>`
            `JsonError` implements `WebResponseError<St, DefaultError>`
          and $N others
  = note: required for `Result<String, MyError>` to implement `Responder`
